  {
   "id": "Lz4Jm2KqAwAJ",
   "from": "Yingbin Zhang",
   "author": "83475948c93daf9d",
   "date": "2017-04-25T03:58:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: Questions about using the createItem() and the mirt.model() at the same time",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Dr. <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Chalmers,<br><br>  I see. <br>  It works well when defining two different custom models.<br>  Thanks for your help!<br></span>  Kind regards.<br><br>Yingbin Zhang</span><br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:medium none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"></pre></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:medium none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:blue\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">P.old2PL &lt;- function(par,Theta,ncat){\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    a1 &lt;- par[1]\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    a2 &lt;- par[2]\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    b  &lt;- par[3]\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    P1 &lt;- 1 / (1 + exp(-1*(a1*Theta[,1] + a2*Theta[,2] - b)))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    cbind(1-P1, P1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">  }\r\n</span><br></pre></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:medium none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px 0px 0px 40px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">name &lt;- &#39;old2PL&#39;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">par &lt;- c(a1 =0.5,a2=0, b = 0)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">est &lt;- c(TRUE, FALSE,TRUE)<br></span>&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\"> x &lt;- createItem(name, par=par, est=est, P=P.old2PL)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><br>&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">name2 &lt;- &#39;old2PL2&#39;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">par2 &lt;- c(a1 =0,a2=0.5, b = 0)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">est2 &lt;- c(FALSE,TRUE, TRUE)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\"> x2 &lt;- createItem(name2, par=par2, est=est2, P=P.old2PL)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><br>&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">sat &lt;- mirt(data, 2, c(rep(&#39;old2PL&#39;,16),rep(&#39;old2PL2&#39;,16)), customItems=list(old2PL=x,old2PL2=x2))\r\n</span>Iteration: 25, Log-Lik: -9695.016, Max-Change: 0.00009\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">coef(sat)\r\n</span>$Item.1\r\n       a1 a2     b\r\npar 0.822  0 1.054\r\n\r\n$Item.2\r\n       a1 a2      b\r\npar 1.486  0 -0.408\r\n\r\n$Item.3\r\n       a1 a2     b\r\npar 1.068  0 1.147<br><br>...<br><br>$Item.16\r\n       a1 a2     b\r\npar 0.691  0 0.384\r\n\r\n$Item.17\r\n    a1    a2      b\r\npar  0 1.351 -4.017\r\n\r\n$Item.18\r\n    a1    a2     b\r\npar  0 1.818 0.925<br><br>......<br><br>$Item.31\r\n    a1    a2      b\r\npar  0 2.197 -2.709\r\n\r\n$Item.32\r\n    a1  a2     b\r\npar  0 0.1 1.649</pre><br>在 2017年4月25日星期二 UTC+8上午10:55:25，Phil Chalmers写道：<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Yingbin,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m fairly certain that custom itemtypes ignore the loadings syntax in mirt.model to build the Q-matrix. After all, you could define a model with no slopes at all, and mirt would have no way of knowing that beforehand. </div><div><br></div><div>You should probably define two different custom models instead with the correct loadings, and supply each correct model to the associated item. HTH.</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
